{
  "slug": "composing-with-pytheory",
  "name": "Composing With Pytheory",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Compose music with PyTheory — progressions, melodies, drums, and full arrangements rendered to audio or MIDI from pure Python.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **6 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (6): `chord-lab-with-pytheory` (Build, voice, and analyze individual chords with PyTheory), `composing-with-pytheory` (Compose music with PyTheory — chord progressions, melodies, basslines, drum grooves, and full multi-part arrangements written in pure…), `keys-and-harmony-with-pytheory` (Analyze and generate keys and chord progressions with PyTheory), `playing-guitar-with-pytheory` (Help guitarists and string players with PyTheory — chord fingerings and shapes, ASCII tablature, chord identification, scale diagrams,…), `scales-modes-and-tunings-with-pytheory` (Explore scales, modes, tones, and tuning systems with PyTheory), `transcription-and-notation-with-pytheory` (Transcribe audio and convert between music formats with PyTheory)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install composing-with-pytheory@claude-community` from `kennethreitz/pytheory-skill` (`plugins/composing-with-pytheory`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
